---
// Imported by path rather than from `@astrojs/starlight/components`, which does
// not re-export it in Starlight 0.41.
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';

// Written into `public/` by `scripts/copy-store.mjs`, which the dev and build
// scripts both run first. The listing is generated from the bundles, so this page
// cannot describe a playbook the store does not actually serve.
import index from '../../public/store/playbooks/index.json';

const entries = [...index.entries].sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));

const title = 'Playbooks store';
const description = 'The playbooks you can install into Llooma, and how to add one.';
---

<StarlightPage frontmatter={{ title, description, tableOfContents: false }}>
	<p>
		A playbook is a procedure the model follows: how a job gets done, written once and switched on in
		any conversation. Where a <a href="/personas/">persona</a> is <em>who</em> is answering, a
		playbook is <em>how</em>. Open the Library, choose <strong>Playbooks store</strong>, and install
		what you want.
	</p>

	<div class="playbook-list not-content">
		{
			entries.map((entry) => (
				<article class="playbook-card">
					<div class="playbook-body">
						<h2>{entry.name}</h2>
						<p class="playbook-summary">{entry.summary}</p>
						{entry.tags.length > 0 && (
							<ul class="playbook-tags">
								{entry.tags.map((tag) => (
									<li>{tag}</li>
								))}
							</ul>
						)}
						<p class="playbook-meta">
							<span>{entry.origin}</span>
							{entry.steps ? <span>{entry.steps} sections</span> : null}
							{entry.author && <span>{entry.author}</span>}
							<a href={`/store/playbooks/${entry.path}`}>bundle</a>
						</p>
					</div>
				</article>
			))
		}
	</div>

	<h2>Adding one</h2>

	<p>
		Write a bundle in <a href="https://github.com/cedhuf/llooma/tree/main/store/playbooks"
			><code>store/playbooks/bundles/</code></a
		>, run <code>pnpm playbooks:index</code>, and open a pull request. The format and the rules are
		in the
		<a href="https://github.com/cedhuf/llooma/blob/main/store/playbooks/README.md"
			>folder's README</a
		>.
	</p>

	<p>
		The ones worth writing say what to establish before starting, what the answer should look like,
		and what <em>not</em> to do, since the failure mode is usually specific. A playbook that only says
		"be helpful" is not a procedure.
	</p>

	<p>
		Playbooks are written in English, for the same reason personas are: the store is read by
		everyone, and a listing half in one language is one nobody can browse. A playbook answers in the
		language of the conversation it is switched on in.
	</p>
</StarlightPage>

<style>
	.playbook-list {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin-block: 1.5rem;
	}

	.playbook-card {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.875rem;
		padding: 1rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
		border-radius: 0.75rem;
		background: var(--sl-color-black);
	}

	.playbook-body {
		min-width: 0;
	}

	.playbook-body h2 {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-base);
		line-height: 1.3;
		border: 0;
	}

	.playbook-summary {
		margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
	}

	.playbook-tags {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.25rem;
		margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}

	.playbook-tags li {
		padding: 0.05rem 0.4rem;
		border-radius: 0.25rem;
		background: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}

	.playbook-meta {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
	}
</style>
